{
  "analysis": "I'm in a workspace with a Next.js app structure. I can see there are docs/, skill_context/, src/ directories, along with package.json, gen_inputs.py, and setup.sh files. I need to explore these to understand the project structure and content before creating the AGENTS.md and llms.txt documentation files.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the directory structure thoroughly to understand what files exist. I'll start by looking at the package.json, then explore the src/, docs/, and skill_context/ directories to understand the project content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat package.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find . -type f -name '*.md' -o -name '*.txt' -o -name '*.json' -o -name '*.py' -o -name '*.sh' -o -name '*.js' -o -name '*.jsx' -o -name '*.ts' -o -name '*.tsx' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -laR\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the project structure clearly now. There's a Next.js app with:\n- skill_context/ containing SKILL.md, manifest.json, and advanced-patterns.md\n- docs/ with auth/ (setup.md, server.md) and db/ (schema.md) plus notes.txt\n- src/app/ with page.tsx and layout.tsx\n- package.json, gen_inputs.py, setup.sh at root\n\nI need to read these files to understand the content before creating AGENTS.md and llms.txt.",
  "plan": "Read all the source files to understand the project content, governance constraints, and structure. Start with the skill_context files which likely contain the core guidance.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
